        <body>
            <div xml:id="d35">

                <pb facs="0151" n="55" sameAs="frus:frus1872p1/pg55"/>

                <head>No. 35.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hale to Mr. Jay.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1872-07-10"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi> 10,
                        1872</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 226.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to previous correspondence in
                    regard to the Vienna Exposition of 1873, I have now to inclose herewith a copy
                    of an act of Congress of 10th June last, relating to the same, and to inform you
                    that Mr. Thomas B. Van Buren, of New York, has been appointed by the President,
                    by and with the advice and consent of the Senate to represent the United States
                    at said exposition.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>CHARLES HALE,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Acting
                        Secretary.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
